<title>ITALY: Italy state industries accept metalworkers deal.</title>
<headline>Italy state industries accept metalworkers deal.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-02-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Intersind, the association representing Italian state industries, said on Tuesday that it had accepted a government proposal to end a pay dispute in the engineering and metalworking industry.</p>
<p>The three unions in the sector, which employs 1.7 million workers, endorsed the deal earlier on Tuesday. The government is still awaiting a response from the biggest employers' organisation, Federmeccanica, expected later on Tuesday.</p>
<p>&quot;Intersind will tell Labour Minister Tiziano Treu that it accepts the proposal mediated by the government and is ready to sign a deal immediately,&quot; Intersind president Agostino Paci said in a statement.</p>
<p>--Rome newsroom +39 6 678 2505</p>
</text>
